{"title":"Teaching","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Teaching","toc":false,"page-layout":"article"},"headingText":"Teaching Philosophy","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\nI aim to connect transportation engineering theory to problems students can see in their\nown cities — congestion, crashes, and unequal access to mobility. My courses combine\nfoundational modeling with hands-on work using real traffic and transit datasets, so\nstudents leave able to apply these methods in practice, not just on exams.\n\n<hr class=\"rule\">\n\n<div class=\"section-label\">Courses Taught</div>\n\n::: {.row-list}\n::: {.row}\n::: {.row-meta}\nFall 2024, Fall 2025\nUndergraduate\n:::\n::: {.row-content}\n### CE 4xx — Transportation Systems Analysis\nIntroduction to traffic flow theory, capacity analysis, and transportation planning\nfundamentals.\n:::\n:::\n\n::: {.row}\n::: {.row-meta}\nSpring 2025, Spring 2026\nGraduate\n:::\n::: {.row-content}\n### CE 5xx — Traffic Flow Theory & Simulation\nMacroscopic and microscopic traffic modeling, calibration, and simulation using SUMO\nand VISSIM.\n:::\n:::\n\n::: {.row}\n::: {.row-meta}\nFall 2025\nGraduate Seminar\n:::\n::: {.row-content}\n### CE 6xx — Data-Driven Transportation Safety\nStatistical and machine-learning approaches to crash prediction and proactive safety\nmanagement, with a semester-long applied project.\n:::\n:::\n:::\n\n<hr class=\"rule\">\n\n::: {.split}\n::: {}\n### Student Mentoring — Ph.D.\n[Student Name] — *[Dissertation Topic]* (expected [Year])\n[Student Name] — *[Dissertation Topic]* (expected [Year])\n\n### Student Mentoring — M.S.\n[Student Name] — *[Thesis Topic]*\n:::\n\n::: {}\n### Alumni\n[Alumnus Name], Ph.D. [Year] — now at [Placement]\n[Alumnus Name], M.S. [Year] — now at [Placement]\n\n### Recruiting\nI am recruiting new Ph.D. and M.S. students interested in traffic systems, safety\nanalytics, and CAV technologies. See [Contact](contact.qmd) for how to apply.\n:::\n:::\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## Teaching Philosophy\n\nI aim to connect transportation engineering theory to problems students can see in their\nown cities — congestion, crashes, and unequal access to mobility. My courses combine\nfoundational modeling with hands-on work using real traffic and transit datasets, so\nstudents leave able to apply these methods in practice, not just on exams.\n\n<hr class=\"rule\">\n\n<div class=\"section-label\">Courses Taught</div>\n\n::: {.row-list}\n::: {.row}\n::: {.row-meta}\nFall 2024, Fall 2025\nUndergraduate\n:::\n::: {.row-content}\n### CE 4xx — Transportation Systems Analysis\nIntroduction to traffic flow theory, capacity analysis, and transportation planning\nfundamentals.\n:::\n:::\n\n::: {.row}\n::: {.row-meta}\nSpring 2025, Spring 2026\nGraduate\n:::\n::: {.row-content}\n### CE 5xx — Traffic Flow Theory & Simulation\nMacroscopic and microscopic traffic modeling, calibration, and simulation using SUMO\nand VISSIM.\n:::\n:::\n\n::: {.row}\n::: {.row-meta}\nFall 2025\nGraduate Seminar\n:::\n::: {.row-content}\n### CE 6xx — Data-Driven Transportation Safety\nStatistical and machine-learning approaches to crash prediction and proactive safety\nmanagement, with a semester-long applied project.\n:::\n:::\n:::\n\n<hr class=\"rule\">\n\n::: {.split}\n::: {}\n### Student Mentoring — Ph.D.\n[Student Name] — *[Dissertation Topic]* (expected [Year])\n[Student Name] — *[Dissertation Topic]* (expected [Year])\n\n### Student Mentoring — M.S.\n[Student Name] — *[Thesis Topic]*\n:::\n\n::: {}\n### Alumni\n[Alumnus Name], Ph.D. [Year] — now at [Placement]\n[Alumnus Name], M.S. [Year] — now at [Placement]\n\n### Recruiting\nI am recruiting new Ph.D. and M.S. students interested in traffic systems, safety\nanalytics, and CAV technologies. See [Contact](contact.qmd) for how to apply.\n:::\n:::\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print"